            "review_title": "Review at The Gioi Hai San 2 (Seafood World 2)",
            "review_text": "G C\nAnchorage, Alaska966 contributions\n0\nExceptionally fresh seafood & excellent service\nApr 2015 • Solo\nOf the 2 The Gioi Hai San seafood restaurants, I've eat at the Hoan Kiem District place twice -- and I've been truly impressed with the exceptional quality of the fresh seafood, the nice atmosphere (& super clean, brightly lit interior w/ large windows looking out onto the street), and the wonderful service that I've received each time. For seafood lovers, Ha Noi offers many great places to dine on fish, crustaceans, and mollusks, and this is one of my favorites. Typically, it's usually a good idea to go with a group of friends, for best enjoyment (as you can order a variety of dishes, each of which has portions beyond the capacity of a single diner)... Many of the fish entrees are priced by the kilogram, so it helps to find out the size of the one(s) that you will be ordering (to avoid a \"surprise\" when the bill shows up). During my last visit, I arrived hungry so that I try the whole steamed pomfret -- it came to my table on a large platter covered with green onions & herbs, simmering in savory soy/ginger broth atop a small burner while I ate. The delightful waitress was really helpful during my meal, as she offered to transfer (boneless) chunks of the delicious fish to my plate, adding the yummy broth to the rice as well, always with a nice smile -- truly wonderful, attentive, and courteous service that will bring me back again to sample more of their great seafood items... enjoy :))\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 20, 2015",
